tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2306281?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jokeren","id":2306281,"login":"Jokeren","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDYyODE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jokeren","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"Hi,\r\nI have implemented the following kernel in Triton. It considers a flat array of 0s, accesses blocks of values, sums across the columns and stores the result. \r\nI am experiencing two issues that I cannot understand under Triton 1.1.1 \r\n\r\n(1) The code below runs fine under Triton 1.1.0. However, it crashes under the 1.1.1 version. <br />\r\nThe error message is `CUDA: Error- misaligned address`.  \r\n\r\n(2)Triton seems formatting specific (?). Indeed if I set `BLOCK_SIZE=128` (or 256) in the code below, the kernel seems to give the expected result with Triton 1.1.1. However, if I now replace the line\r\n`inputs = tl.load(input_ptr + offsets[:, None] + indices[None, :])`\r\nby\r\n```\r\ninputs = tl.load(\r\n    input_ptr + offsets[:, None] + indices[None, :]\r\n)\r\n```\r\nI obtain the same `CUDA: Error- misaligned address` crash.\r\n\r\n <br />\r\nI cannot understand why these issues happen. Do you have any thoughts? <br />\r\nThanks for your help 🙏, <br />\r\nAntoine\r\n\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\nHere is the code I am running:\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport torch\r\nimport triton\r\nimport triton.language as tl\r\nprint(\"Triton version\", triton.__version__)\r\n    \r\n@triton.jit\r\ndef kernel(\r\n    input_ptr,\r\n    indices_ptr,\r\n    offsets_ptr,\r\n    output_ptr,\r\n    **meta,\r\n):\r\n    # Thread param\r\n    output_id = tl.program_id(0)\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE = meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"] \r\n    BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES = meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES\"]\r\n\r\n    # Load offsets\r\n    output_range = output_id * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\r\n    offsets = tl.load(offsets_ptr + output_range)\r\n\r\n    # Load indices\r\n    indices_range = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES)\r\n    indices = tl.load(indices_ptr + indices_range)\r\n\r\n    # Load input\r\n    inputs = tl.load(input_ptr + offsets[:, None] + indices[None, :])\r\n    sum_inputs = tl.sum(inputs, 1)\r\n\r\n    # Result\r\n    tl.store(output_ptr + output_range, sum_inputs + 0.0)   \r\n\r\ntorch.manual_seed(0)\r\nx_size, y_size, z_size = 50, 50, 50\r\noutput_size = (256,)\r\nt_input = torch.zeros(x_size * y_size * z_size, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int8)\r\nt_indices = torch.randint(low=0, high=(x_size - 1) * y_size * z_size, size=(128,), device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int64)\r\nt_offset = torch.randint(low=0, high=y_size * z_size, size=output_size, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int64)\r\nt_output = torch.zeros(output_size, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.float32) - 1000\r\n\r\n# Works for triton 1.1.0 but not for 1.1.1\r\nBLOCK_SIZE = 8\r\nkernel[((t_offset.shape[0] // BLOCK_SIZE),)](\r\n    t_input,\r\n    t_indices,\r\n    t_offset,\r\n    t_output,\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES=t_indices.shape[0] # 128\r\n)\r\nassert (t_output == 0).all(), \"Should be all 0s\"\r\n```","closed_at":"2023-02-18T02:01:45Z","closed_by":{"ava