thor_association":"NONE","body":"Thank you @ptillet for your answer. After installing triton 2.0.0 via `pip install triton==2.0.0.dev20220206` I still run into the format-specific issue (2).\r\nFor reproducibility, I am running\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport torch\r\nimport triton\r\nimport triton.language as tl\r\nprint(\"Triton version\", triton.__version__)\r\n    \r\n@triton.jit\r\ndef kernel(\r\n    input_ptr,\r\n    indices_ptr,\r\n    offsets_ptr,\r\n    output_ptr,\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES: tl.constexpr,\r\n):\r\n    # Thread param\r\n    output_id = tl.program_id(0)\r\n\r\n    # Load offsets\r\n    output_range = output_id * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\r\n    offsets = tl.load(offsets_ptr + output_range)\r\n\r\n    # Load indices\r\n    indices_range = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES)\r\n    indices = tl.load(indices_ptr + indices_range)\r\n\r\n    # Load input\r\n    inputs = tl.load(\r\n        input_ptr + offsets[:, None] + indices[None, :]\r\n    )\r\n    sum_inputs = tl.sum(inputs, 1)\r\n\r\n    # Result\r\n    tl.store(output_ptr + output_range, sum_inputs + 0.0)   \r\n\r\ntorch.manual_seed(0)\r\nx_size, y_size, z_size = 50, 50, 50\r\noutput_size = (256,)\r\nt_input = torch.zeros(x_size * y_size * z_size, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int8)\r\nt_indices = torch.randint(low=0, high=(x_size - 1) * y_size * z_size, size=(128,), device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int64)\r\nt_offset = torch.randint(low=0, high=y_size * z_size, size=output_size, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.int64)\r\nt_output = torch.zeros(output_size, device=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.float32) - 1000\r\n\r\n# Works for triton 1.1.0 but not for 1.1.1\r\nBLOCK_SIZE = 8\r\nkernel[((t_offset.shape[0] // BLOCK_SIZE),)](\r\n    t_input,\r\n    t_indices,\r\n    t_offset,\r\n    t_output,\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\r\n    BLOCK_SIZE_INDICES=t_indices.shape[0] # 128\r\n)\r\nassert (t_output == 0).all(), \"Should be all 0s\"\r\n```\r\nand I obtain `CUDA error: misaligned ad